<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 https://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

    <parent>
        <groupId>eu.wohlben</groupId>
        <artifactId>qits</artifactId>
        <version>2026.917.31410</version>
        <relativePath>../pom.xml</relativePath>
    </parent>

    <!-- PUBLISHED COORDINATES, and they deliberately do not inherit the parent's.
         `eu.wohlben.qits:qits-*` is what every artifact this platform releases is called
         (qits-auth-core, qits-db-core, qits-eventstream, qits-workspace-daemon-protocol), and this
         module joined them the day qits-ci started taking the daemon version from a released
         dependency instead of a configuration entry — see CiDaemonBinary.

         The artifactId gains the `qits-` prefix the directory does not because the directory name
         is a path in one reactor and the coordinate is a name in a registry shared by every
         repository here; `ci-daemon-protocol` in a global namespace says nothing about whose ci.
         It is also the name the coordinate ALREADY HAS on the consumer's side: qits-ci's vendored
         copy of this module is `eu.wohlben.qits:qits-ci-daemon-protocol` in its own reactor today,
         so the published jar takes that name as the vendored copy is deleted and the dependency
         resolves to this artifact without a single call site changing. Two artifacts under one
         coordinate with two owners is the state that rename avoids. -->
    <groupId>eu.wohlben.qits</groupId>
    <artifactId>qits-ci-daemon-protocol</artifactId>

    <!-- The ci-daemon control-socket wire contract: plain records + enums + the shared type/field
         name constants, framework-free and dependency-free. Both qits-ci (the host, serializing
         with Jackson) and the native binary (`ci-daemon`, mapping via Vert.x JsonObject) depend on
         it so neither owns the protocol. No JSON library here on purpose — serialization lives on
         each side against whatever it already carries.

         Deliberately NOT the workspace-daemon protocol: the messages are disjoint, and coupling
         the two repos' wire contracts would make every workspace capability bump a ci event
         (finish-ci-feature.md §3).

         IT CARRIES THE RELEASE'S OWN VERSION TOO (CiDaemonBinary), which is why it is the module
         that gets deployed rather than a second "pin" jar beside it: the thing a consumer must pin
         and the thing it must speak are the same release, and one artifact cannot ship half of that
         pair. -->

    <dependencies>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.junit.jupiter</groupId>
            <artifactId>junit-jupiter</artifactId>
            <scope>test</scope>
        </dependency>
    </dependencies>

    <build>
        <!-- FILTERING IS ON FOR THIS MODULE'S ONE RESOURCE AND NOTHING ELSE. The include/exclude
             pair is not belt-and-braces: filtering every resource would rewrite any future wire
             fixture that happens to contain `${`, and this module is the wire contract — a corrupt
             fixture here is a wrong assertion, not a build error. CiDaemonBinary refuses an
             unfiltered value, so switching this block off fails loudly rather than shipping the
             literal `${project.version}` as the path segment a step container downloads its binary
             from. -->
        <resources>
            <resource>
                <directory>src/main/resources</directory>
                <filtering>true</filtering>
                <includes>
                    <include>eu/wohlben/qits/cidaemon/protocol/ci-daemon-binary.properties</include>
                </includes>
            </resource>
            <resource>
                <directory>src/main/resources</directory>
                <filtering>false</filtering>
                <excludes>
                    <exclude>eu/wohlben/qits/cidaemon/protocol/ci-daemon-binary.properties</exclude>
                </excludes>
            </resource>
        </resources>
        <plugins>
            <plugin>
                <artifactId>maven-compiler-plugin</artifactId>
            </plugin>
            <plugin>
                <artifactId>maven-surefire-plugin</artifactId>
            </plugin>
        </plugins>
    </build>
</project>
